 is the new industry standard. Every competitor reports BEAM scores. Scaling behavior is where graph memory should differentiate from flat vector stores."}]}],"id":"blk-78258","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-78260","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-141691","text":"Session 2: MemoryAgentBench"}]},{"id":"blk-78261","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141692","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-141693","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141694","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_8889e094cb2b904d65f6a29cd7861f1c"}]}],"id":"blk-78262","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141695","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-141696","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.05257"}]}],"id":"blk-78264","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141697","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repo"},{"id":"spn-141698","text":": https://github.com/HUST-AI-HYZ/MemoryAgentBench"}]}],"id":"blk-78266","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141699","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-141700","text":": Multi-turn incremental format, includes EventQA and FactConsolidation"}]}],"id":"blk-78268","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141701","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-141702","text":": 4 competency scores — accurate retrieval, test-time learning, long-range understanding, selective forgetting"}]}],"id":"blk-78270","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141703","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-141704","text":": Multi-turn format requires simulating incremental store→query cycles, not batch ingest. Map \"selective forgetting\" to "},{"id":"spn-141705","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_by_policy"},{"id":"spn-141706","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-141707","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_node"},{"id":"spn-141708","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-78272","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141709","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-141710","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141711","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memoryagentbench"}]}],"id":"blk-78274","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141712","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-141713","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141714","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memoryagentbench --limit 50"}]}],"id":"blk-78276","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141715","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why second"},{"id":"spn-141716","text":": Directly tests Graphonomous's differentiating features (forgetting, learning loop). ICLR 2026 paper — high credibility."}]}],"id":"blk-78278","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-78280","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-141717","text":"Session 3: LMEB (Long-horizon Memory Embedding Benchmark)"}]},{"id":"blk-78281","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141718","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-141719","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141720","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_81c0f91f92b9b4a52e0a38b44c49a492"}]}],"id":"blk-78282","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141721","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-141722","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12572"}]}],"id":"blk-78284","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78287","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141723","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repo"},{"id":"spn-141724","text":": https://github.com/KaLM-Embedding/LMEB"}]}],"id":"blk-78286","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141725","marks":["bold"],"text":"HuggingFace"},{"id":"spn-141726","text":": https://huggingface.co/datasets/KaLM-Embedding/LMEB"}]}],"id":"blk-78288","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141727","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-141728","text":": 22 datasets, 193 zero-shot retrieval tasks across 4 memory types (episodic, dialogue, semantic, procedural)"}]}],"id":"blk-78290","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78293","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141729","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-141730","text":": Retrieval accuracy per memory type, aggregate score"}]}],"id":"blk-78292","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78295","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141731","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-141732","text":": This benchmarks the "},{"id":"spn-141733","marks":["italic"],"text":"embedding model"},{"id":"spn-141734","text":", not the full system. Run nomic-embed-text-v2-moe through the LMEB eval harness (likely Python). May need a thin Python wrapper or direct Elixir port of the eval logic."}]}],"id":"blk-78294","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78297","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141735","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-141736","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141737","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lmeb"}]}],"id":"blk-78296","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78299","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141738","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-141739","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141740","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lmeb --model nomic-embed-text-v2-moe"}]}],"id":"blk-78298","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141741","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why third"},{"id":"spn-141742","text":": Cheapest to run (embedding-only, no LLM judge needed). Validates the foundational layer. If nomic scores poorly on memory-specific retrieval, that's a critical finding."}]}],"id":"blk-78300","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-78302","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-141743","text":"Session 4: MemoryBench (Continual Learning from Feedback)"}]},{"id":"blk-78303","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141744","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-141745","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141746","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_8ef86ae124eb2f03375289107dcac5ae"}]}],"id":"blk-78304","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78307","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141747","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-141748","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.17281"}]}],"id":"blk-78306","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78309","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141749","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-141750","text":": User feedback simulation across multiple domains and languages"}]}],"id":"blk-78308","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78311","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141751","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-141752","text":": Continual learning accuracy, feedback utilization rate, cross-domain transfer"}]}],"id":"blk-78310","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141753","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-141754","text":": Requires simulating the feedback loop — "},{"id":"spn-141755","marks":["code"],"text":"learn_from_feedback"},{"id":"spn-141756","text":" with explicit/action-based/implicit feedback types, then re-querying to measure improvement. Multi-domain and multilingual means varied corpus."}]}],"id":"blk-78312","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141757","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-141758","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141759","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memorybench"}]}],"id":"blk-78314","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78317","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141760","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-141761","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141762","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memorybench --domain all --limit 100"}]}],"id":"blk-78316","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78319","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141763","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why fourth"},{"id":"spn-141764","text":": Directly tests the learning loop. Published finding that no system beats RAG baseline — if Graphonomous does, that's a headline result."}]}],"id":"blk-78318","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-78320","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-141765","text":"Session 5: LifeBench (Non-Declarative Memory)"}]},{"id":"blk-78321","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78323","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141766","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-141767","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141768","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_824059ff9230ff0953646ea7ac2e7d6a"}]}],"id":"blk-78322","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78325","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141769","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-141770","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.03781"}]}],"id":"blk-78324","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78327","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141771","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-141772","text":": Long-horizon event simulations with real-world priors (surveys, maps, calendars)"}]}],"id":"blk-78326","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78329","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141773","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-141774","text":": Accuracy on habitual/procedural memory inference, declarative vs non-declarative breakdown"}]}],"id":"blk-78328","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78331","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141775","marks":["bold"],"text":"SOTA"},{"id":"spn-141776","text":": 55.2% (top system)"}]}],"id":"blk-78330","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141777","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-141778","text":": Tests "},{"id":"spn-141779","marks":["italic"],"text":"inferred"},{"id":"spn-141780","text":" knowledge, not explicitly stored facts. Graphonomous procedural nodes + edge patterns may capture habitual patterns that flat stores miss. May need to extend "},{"id":"spn-141781","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_procedural"},{"id":"spn-141782","text":" or add inference logic."}]}],"id":"blk-78332","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78335","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141783","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-141784","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141785","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lifebench"}]}],"id":"blk-78334","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78337","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141786","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-141787","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141788","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lifebench --limit 50"}]}],"id":"blk-78336","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141789","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why fifth"},{"id":"spn-141790","text":": Hardest benchmark (SOTA is 55%). Low expectations, high signal. If graph structure helps even marginally on non-declarative memory, that validates the architecture thesis."}]}],"id":"blk-78338","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-78340","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-141791","text":"Session 6: AMemGym (On-Policy Interactive)"}]},{"id":"blk-78341","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141792","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-141793","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141794","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_b7ccffd9e67df8e7b42366ff24a9be82"}]}],"id":"blk-78342","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141795","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-141796","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.01966"}]}],"id":"blk-78344","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78347","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141797","marks":["bold"],"text":"HuggingFace"},{"id":"spn-141798","text":": https://huggingface.co/datasets/AGI-Eval/AMemGym"}]}],"id":"blk-78346","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141799","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-141800","text":": Interactive on-policy benchmark — agent generates its own conversation"}]}],"id":"blk-78348","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78351","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141801","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-141802","text":": Structured state consistency, memory utilization, persona tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-78350","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141803","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-141804","text":": This is fundamentally different from other benchmarks. The agent must "},{"id":"spn-141805","marks":["italic"],"text":"participate"},{"id":"spn-141806","text":" in the conversation, not just answer post-hoc questions. Requires wiring Graphonomous MCP into a simulated conversation loop with an LLM-simulated user. Most complex harness to build."}]}],"id":"blk-78352","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141807","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-141808","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141809","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.amemgym"}]}],"id":"blk-78354","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78357","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141810","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-141811","text":": "},{"id":"spn-141812","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.amemgym --scenarios 10"}]}],"id":"blk-78356","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141813","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why last"},{"id":"spn-141814","text":": Most complex integration. Requires LLM-in-the-loop (simulated user). But the most realistic test of how Graphonomous actually performs in production. Save for last when all other harnesses are proven."}]}],"id":"blk-78358","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-78360","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-141815","text":"Post-Completion"}]},{"id":"blk-78361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141816","text":"After all 6 harnesses are built and run:"}]},{"id":"blk-78362","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141817","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-141818","marks":["code"],"text":"OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"},{"id":"spn-141819","text":" with a unified results table"}]}],"id":"blk-78363","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141820","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-141821","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.com/benchmarks/"},{"id":"spn-141822","text":" pages with new benchmark results"}]}],"id":"blk-78365","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141823","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-141824","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/site/portfolio-review.html"},{"id":"spn-141825","text":" competitive landscape"}]}],"id":"blk-78367","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141826","text":"Store a comprehensive episodic node in Graphonomous summarizing the full evaluation"}]}],"id":"blk-78369","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141827","text":"Consider adding top-line scores to "},{"id":"spn-141828","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/README.md"}]}],"id":"blk-78371","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-78373","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-141829","text":"Anti-Patterns to Avoid"}]},{"id":"blk-78374","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141830","text":"Do NOT modify "},{"id":"spn-141831","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-141832","text":" or the retrieval pipeline to game a specific benchmark"}]}],"id":"blk-78375","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141833","text":"Do NOT add benchmark-specific code paths to the core engine"}]}],"id":"blk-78377","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141834","text":"Do NOT skip the smoke test ("},{"id":"spn-141835","marks":["code"],"text":"--limit 50"},{"id":"spn-141836","text":") before full runs"}]}],"id":"blk-78379","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141837","text":"Do NOT fabricate competitive baselines — only cite published numbers with sources"}]}],"id":"blk-78381","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-78384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-141838","text":"Do NOT skip storing results in Graphonomous — the learning loop is the point"}]}],"id":"blk-78383","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraxs4bhngew33kkukkw2jibpemwi5ps4t5g6zzknexnt4cmeylm7ra","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}